{"skill":{"slug":"docker-compose","displayName":"Docker Compose"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770692540221,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2680,"sha256":"f8881a8c4a94b30da8fbe14004eeeb1d4cee5659c323f400ee92b14ec641758e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1914,"sha256":"d137e4b7e4247f840450e5f3ea4dc74b6846d1fc362e259ecbe92f4b67214779","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789057098863,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d1de2381b23a3841e5045154e17a22784a576cb5c85a5a71b1976ecb2921a726","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d1de2381b23a3841e5045154e17a22784a576cb5c85a5a71b1976ecb2921a726","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: docker-compose\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides documentation and best practices for Docker Compose. The `SKILL.md` file contains educational content, including warnings about `docker compose down -v` and advice on using `.dockerignore` for security, as well as managing environment variables and resource limits. There is no evidence of malicious instructions, data exfiltration attempts, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection with harmful intent. All content is aligned with the stated purpose of educating about Docker Compose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162661005},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789057098863},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill provides Docker Compose configuration guidance and does not include executable code or hidden behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Docker Compose use can affect local containers, networks, volumes, and environment variables, but this is expected for the skill's purpose and the text explicitly warns about destructive volume deletion and secret handling.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file with metadata declaring Docker/Docker Compose as relevant binaries; no install script, package dependency, or remote retrieval is present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Instructions are scoped to composing container configuration and warnings; there are no role changes, prompt overrides, hidden directives, or requests to bypass user control.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, background worker, scheduled task, privilege escalation, credential harvesting, or automatic command execution is included.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Docker Compose guidance, and the artifact content matches that purpose with advice on healthchecks, volumes, resource limits, .dockerignore, overrides, profiles, and environment precedence.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before using generated Docker Compose changes, review volume commands carefully, especially `docker compose down -v`, and confirm secrets are excluded from images and base compose files. The skill itself is advisory and proportionate to Docker Compose work.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789057098863}}}}}